From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:42:10 +0200
Subject: riscv: dts: sophgo: add a Milk-V Duo S C906L overlay

The previous patch disables the C906L coprocessor and deletes its
reserved-memory region, because Armbian ships no FreeRTOS image for it. That is
the right default and the wrong permanent answer: the core is the whole point of
Milk-V's "Arduino on the Duo", and somebody with a cvirtos.elf should be able to
turn it back on without rebuilding a kernel.

So put the two nodes back in an overlay, selectable at boot with

    overlays=c906l

in /boot/armbianEnv.txt. The region is pinned at CVIMMAP_FREERTOS_ADDR from the
vendor's cvi_board_memmap.h, which is where a vendor-SDK firmware expects to be
loaded. That is 0x9fe00000, the top 2MiB of the 512MiB the board DTS declares.

Note the node is named region@9fe00000 here, not region@8fe00000 as in the
sg2000.dtsi this restores it to. That node carries reg = <0x9fe00000 0x200000>
under an @8fe00000 name - a mismatch arm64 does not share. reg is what reserves
the memory, so the name is the part that is wrong; this overlay is consistent.

The composite sg2000-milkv-duo-s-c906l.dtb target is never booted. It is there
so the build applies the overlay to the base with fdtoverlay, which validates
that the overlay still fits its base on every build, and - through the
base-dtb-y rule in scripts/Makefile.dtbs - is what makes the base DTB get -@.
Without those symbols U-Boot's "fdt apply" cannot resolve &remoteproc and the
overlay is unusable at runtime.

The #address-cells/#size-cells restated in the fragment match the base node.
They are only there to stop dtc warning about the reg length: compiling an
overlay on its own, it cannot see the target's cell counts and assumes <2>/<1>.

Verified with scripts/dtc/fdtoverlay on both architectures: the region returns
at 0x9fe00000 with no-map, and c906l-rproc comes back with status = "okay" and
a memory-region pointing at it.

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/Makefile                  |  9 ++
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/overlay/sg2000-c906l.dtso | 51 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/Makefile b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/Makefile
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/Makefile
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/Makefile
@@ -8,3 +8,12 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO) += sg2042-milkv-pioneer.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO) += sg2042-evb-v1.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO) += sg2042-evb-v2.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO) += sg2044-sophgo-srd3-10.dtb
+
+# The C906L coprocessor overlay, selectable at runtime through armbianEnv.txt.
+# The composite target below is never booted: it exists so the build applies the
+# overlay to the base with fdtoverlay, which both validates that it still fits
+# and is what makes Makefile.dtbs pass -@ to the base DTB. Without those
+# symbols, "fdt apply" in U-Boot cannot resolve &remoteproc at boot.
+sg2000-milkv-duo-s-c906l-dtbs := sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dtb overlay/sg2000-c906l.dtbo
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO) += sg2000-milkv-duo-s-c906l.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO) += overlay/sg2000-c906l.dtbo
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/overlay/sg2000-c906l.dtso b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/overlay/sg2000-c906l.dtso
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..111111111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/overlay/sg2000-c906l.dtso
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0 OR MIT)
+/*
+ * Milk-V Duo S: hand the C906L coprocessor back to Linux.
+ *
+ * The SG2000 carries a second, much smaller RISC-V core (C906L) meant for
+ * real-time work with no operating system in the way - it is what Milk-V's
+ * "Arduino on the Duo" runs sketches on, under FreeRTOS. remoteproc is how
+ * Linux loads firmware onto it and starts it.
+ *
+ * The base device tree disables it and deletes its reserved-memory region,
+ * because Armbian builds no FreeRTOS image and installs no cvirtos.elf, so the
+ * core never starts and the region is 2MiB of a 512MiB board held for nothing.
+ * This overlay puts both back for people who do have firmware to run.
+ *
+ * Enable with, in /boot/armbianEnv.txt:
+ *
+ *     overlays=c906l
+ *
+ * Then put your firmware at /lib/firmware/cvirtos.elf. Without it remoteproc
+ * still registers and simply reports the missing file:
+ *
+ *     remoteproc remoteproc0: c906l-rproc is available
+ *     remoteproc remoteproc0: Direct firmware load for cvirtos.elf failed with error -2
+ *
+ * The region is fixed at the top of DRAM to match CVIMMAP_FREERTOS_ADDR in the
+ * vendor's cvi_board_memmap.h, which is where the FSBL would load a C906L image
+ * from fip.bin, so a firmware built by the vendor SDK expects it there.
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+/plugin/;
+
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	/*
+	 * Restated to match the base node. dtc cannot see the target's cell counts
+	 * when an overlay is compiled on its own, and defaults to <2>/<1>, which
+	 * makes it warn that this reg is the wrong length.
+	 */
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <1>;
+
+	coprocessor_rtos: region@9fe00000 {
+		reg = <0x9fe00000 0x200000>;
+		no-map;
+	};
+};
+
+&remoteproc {
+	memory-region = <&coprocessor_rtos>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
Armbian

